media: i2c: ov5647: pass dev to ov5647_init_controls()

Stable commit 2dedda97a64e ("media: i2c: ov5647: Initialize subdev before
controls") moves the ov5647_init_controls() call in ov5647_probe() after
v4l2_i2c_subdev_init(), so ov5647_init_controls() can use the subdev data.

In rpi-6.12.y, ov5647_init_controls() takes an additional struct device
argument, used to parse the fwnode properties of the sensor. The conflict
resolution drops the old call site, but the moved call merges without
conflict using the upstream single-argument signature, which fails to
build:

  error: too few arguments to function 'ov5647_init_controls'

Pass dev to the moved call, as the rpi-6.12.y call did.

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/ov5647.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/ov5647.c
@@ -1425,7 +1425,7 @@
 	sd->internal_ops = &ov5647_subdev_internal_ops;
 	sd->flags |= V4L2_SUBDEV_FL_HAS_DEVNODE | V4L2_SUBDEV_FL_HAS_EVENTS;
 
-	ret = ov5647_init_controls(sensor);
+	ret = ov5647_init_controls(sensor, dev);
 	if (ret)
 		goto mutex_destroy;
 
